Following the service of Remembrance at the Cross of Sacrifice and the Roll of Honour, a wreath laying ceremony will take place, where wreaths will be laid by representatives of HM Government, Members of the Legislative Assembly, the uniformed services, the Royal British Legion, the Falkland Islands Association and other organisations. A wreath will also be laid by a representative of the families of those who died during the conflict. After the wreath laying ceremony, the service will continue in the Cathedral where there will be a sermon by the Right Reverend Dr David Chillingworth followed by prayers and hymns, and the service will conclude with the blessing of the congregation by Reverend Canon Paul Kerr. Following the service, there will be an opportunity for members of the congregation and the public to view the Roll of Honour at the Cross of Sacrifice.

The Falkland Islands Government has been informed that the following official representatives from UK Government Departments and the Armed Forces will be attending:

* Minister for the Armed Forces, Penny Mordaunt MP;

* Chief of the Defence Staff, General Sir Nicholas Houghton;

* Chief of the General Staff, General Sir Peter Wall;

